{
  "dom_id": "step-q83902",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=6).$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{8}$ | $1$ |",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {0,2,4,6}) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=2)+P(X=4)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {0,2,4})+P(X=6) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=6) & =F(6)-F(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
